\f1\fs22 When Hayley alighted from the ground cab at Koalemos\'92s police cordon around the mansion in the Ghetto, she heard the same noise coming from above the Layer, and shivered. In no uncertain terms, the ice in her bowels informed her bioeme, which sent a telegraph to the more primitive parts of her brain which, in turn, dispatched a message to her visual cortex for an image it could terrify her heart and soul with. Success. In mind\'92s eye, Hayley recalled the PAPER gunship strafing the apartment from which she narrowly escaped. Her fear piqued, it was all she could do to stop from throwing herself to the ground, expecting particle blasts to disintegrate the ground car.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>With more steel than she knew her bones possessed, she ducked under the cordon, flashed her badge and set about finding Koalemos.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Koalemos found her first.
